><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAGUCHI KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ONMORI SHOZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKANO ATUSI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASHIKAWA, TERUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAGUCHI, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ONMORI, SHOZO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKANO, ATUSI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>The opposite sides of an opening (14) in the front of a cassette case (10a) are formed with tape guides (18) each having a guide surface (18a), and in the opening (14) a magnetic tape (T) is stretched between the guide surfaces (18a).  The back (18b) of the guide surface (18a) of the tape guide (18) is formed with a cam groove (26) for guiding an opening/closing lid (320) covering the stretched magnetic tape (T).  Provided below the back (18b) and rearwardly of the cam groove (26) is a projection (28) having a position detecting hole (28a). Sink preventing recesses are provided only in two places, one located forwardly of the cam groove (26) of the back (18b) and the other located rearwardly of the cam groove (26) of the back (18b) and above the projection (28).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Les côtés opposés d'une ouverture (14) ménagée sur l'avant d'un boîtier (10a) de cassette présentent des guides de bande (18), chacun d'entre eux comprenant une surface de guidage (18a). Une bande magnétique (T) s'étire par ailleurs entre les surfaces de guidage (18a) de plusieurs de ces guides, à l'intérieur de ladite ouverture (14). L'arrière (18b) de la surface de guidage (18a) de chaque guide de bande (18) présente une rainure came (26), destinée à guider un couvercle d'ouverture/de fermeture (320) qui recouvre la bande magnétique étirée (T). Sous la partie arrière (18b) de cette rainure came (26) et derrière celle-ci, une protubérance (28) présente un orifice (28a) de détection de position. Enfin, des renfoncements empêchant tout affaissement sont ménagés à deux emplacements, un à l'avant de la rainure came (26) de ladite partie arrière (18b), et l'autre à l'arrière de la rainure came (26) de cette partie arrière (18b), au-dessus de la protubérance (28).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>